## 3.3 Theorem 1: The Tzolk'in-Mars Absorption Identity
We prove that because the Mars cycle is a multiple of the ritual cycle, any day count that resets Mars automatically resets the Tzolk'in.

theorem tzolkin_mars_absorption (d : ℕ) (h_mars : (d : ZMod mars_period) = 0) : 
    (d : ZMod tzolkin_period) = 0 := by
  -- Convert ZMod hypothesis into divisibility statement in Nat
  have div_mars : mars_period ∣ d := by
    exact (ZMod.natCast_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd d mars_period).mp h_mars
    
  -- State the arithmetic fact that 260 divides 780
  have mars_factor : tzolkin_period ∣ mars_period := by
    exact show 260 ∣ 780 by decide
    
  -- Transitivity of divisibility: if 260 | 780 and 780 | d, then 260 | d
  have div_tzolkin : tzolkin_period ∣ d := Nat.dvd_trans mars_factor div_mars
  
  -- Inject back into ZMod space
  exact (ZMod.natCast_zmod_eq_zero_iff_dvd d tzolkin_period).mpr div_tzolkin

