## 4. Discussion & The Future of Ethnomathematics
Historically, interactive theorem proving has focused almost exclusively on modern or Eurocentric mathematics. By implementing this codebase, we demonstrate that ancient non-Western systems are easily and elegantly expressible within modern constructive logic.
Sak Tahn Waax operated without digital computing hardware, yet the equations scrawled on the stucco walls of Xultun obeyed the exact laws of modular arithmetic and divisibility that underpin computer science today. Formalizing these frameworks actively protects indigenous scientific achievements from being minimized as mere "mysticism," elevating them to their proper status as rigorous number theory.
